        <name>LoopVectorizeOptions</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::LoopVectorizeOptions::LoopVectorizeOptions</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>The current defaults when creating the pass with no arguments are: EnableLoopInterleaving = true and EnableLoopVectorization = true. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This means that interleaving default is consistent with the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1cl_1_1opt" kindref="compound">cl::opt</ref> flag, while vectorization is not. FIXME: The default for EnableLoopVectorization in the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1cl_1_1opt" kindref="compound">cl::opt</ref> should be set to true, and the corresponding change to account for this be made in opt.cpp. The initializations below will become: InterleaveOnlyWhenForced(!EnableLoopInterleaving) VectorizeOnlyWhenForced(!EnableLoopVectorization). </para>
        </detaileddescription>
